=========================================================================
PLAIN-LANGUAGE SUMMARY (non-binding — for convenience only)
=========================================================================
Anyone, including for-profit companies, may use, run, and modify this
software for FREE for their own internal and business purposes — including
using it to build, test, secure, or audit their own products and services,
even products and services they sell. That internal use is, and stays, free.

What you may NOT do without buying a separate commercial license is make
money FROM THE SOFTWARE ITSELF: you may not sell it, charge for it, ship it
inside a product or service that is sold, or run it to deliver its
functionality to other people as a paid or commercial service (this includes
hosted, cloud, SaaS, API, and managed-service delivery — even if you never
hand anyone a copy of the code).

You may share and fork the software for free, but you must keep this license
and credit the original "safer-dependencies" project, and say so if you
changed it.

This summary is a friendly overview, not the contract. If anything here
differs from the numbered Sections below, the numbered Sections control. This
is intentionally NOT an OSI-approved "open source" license: the commercial
limitation in Section 4 is a field-of-use limitation.

