8. Termination
   (a) Commercial breach: any act prohibited by Section 4 terminates all
       rights granted to You under this license immediately and
       automatically, without a cure period.
   (b) Attribution / notice breach: any breach of Section 5 terminates Your
       rights, but Your rights are automatically reinstated if You cure the
       breach within 30 days after You become aware of it or are notified by
       the Licensor, provided this is Your first such breach; for repeated or
       willful breaches, Your rights may be terminated without reinstatement.
   (c) Discretionary reinstatement: rights terminated under 8(a), or not
       automatically reinstated under 8(b), may be reinstated only by the
       Licensor in writing.
   (d) Cease use: upon termination You must immediately stop all use,
       distribution, and commercialization of the Software and destroy all
       copies in Your possession or control, except to the extent Section 5(e)
       and Section 10 provide that obligations survive. Copies and derivatives that
       remain within a Commercial Product after termination are unlicensed
       and infringing.
   (e) Downstream protection: each time the Software or a derivative is
       distributed, each recipient automatically receives a license directly
       from the Licensor on these same terms. You may not sublicense and may
       not impose additional or different terms. Termination of Your rights
       does not, by itself, terminate the rights of a good-faith downstream
       recipient who is in compliance.

